---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';

const { googleAnalyticsId, microsoftClarityId, cloudflareAnalyticsToken } = SITE.analytics;
const analyticsEnabled = Boolean(
  googleAnalyticsId || microsoftClarityId || cloudflareAnalyticsToken
);
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles personal data — analytics, newsletter emails, cookies, retention, and your rights under GDPR and CCPA.`}
  lede="What we collect, why, and what you can do about it."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-02')}
>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-warning)]/40 bg-[var(--color-warning)]/10 p-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
    <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Note:</strong> this policy describes what this site
    actually does. It is written in good faith but it is not legal advice. If you operate
    this site, have it reviewed against your deployed configuration before relying on it.
  </div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.organization.legalName} publishes <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> — AI news, tools
    coverage, tutorials and reviews. The site is operated by
    <strong>{SITE.organization.operatedBy ?? SITE.organization.legalName}</strong>
    {SITE.organization.address
      ? `, based in ${SITE.organization.address.locality}, ${SITE.organization.address.countryName}`
      : ''}, which is the data controller for any personal data described below.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any privacy question or data request, email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a>
    {SITE.organization.telephone ? ` or call ${SITE.organization.telephone}` : ''}. Full
    contact routes are on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
  <!--
    Owner: if you are required to publish a full registered street address, a company
    registration number, or a named Data Protection Officer / EU-UK representative, add
    them here. Locality and country are set in src/config/site.config.ts.
  -->

  <h2>How the site is hosted</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is a <strong>static site</strong>. Pages are pre-built and served as files
    from a content delivery network. There is no reader account system, no login, no
    comment database holding your identity, and no server-side profile of you. The
    practical consequence is that there is very little for us to collect in the first
    place.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email address</strong> — only if you subscribe to the AIInsider Briefing. It
      is used to send that newsletter and nothing else. We do not add subscribers to any
      other list, and we do not share the list with tool vendors or advertisers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Correspondence</strong> — if you email the desk, we keep your message and
      address so we can reply, track a correction, or process a directory submission.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Directory and prompt submissions</strong> — the product details and contact
      details you send us when proposing a listing for the
      <a href="/tools/">tool directory</a>, the <a href="/agents/">agent directory</a> or
      the <a href="/prompts/">prompt library</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Server and CDN logs</strong> — our hosting provider records IP addresses,
      user agents, timestamps and requested URLs to serve the page, mitigate abuse and
      absorb denial-of-service traffic. We do not use these logs to identify individual
      readers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference</strong> — stored in your browser's local storage, never
      transmitted to us. Details in the <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This codebase supports three optional analytics providers. Each is
    <strong>off unless an ID is configured</strong>, and when it is off, no script is
    injected and the provider's servers are never contacted from your browser.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — aggregate page views, referrers, approximate
      country and device class. Optional.
      {googleAnalyticsId ? ' Currently enabled.' : ' Currently disabled.'}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> — aggregate interaction and scroll data used to
      find broken layouts and unreadable pages. Optional.
      {microsoftClarityId ? ' Currently enabled.' : ' Currently disabled.'}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — privacy-preserving, cookieless page-view
      counting. Optional.
      {cloudflareAnalyticsToken ? ' Currently enabled.' : ' Currently disabled.'}
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    {
      analyticsEnabled
        ? 'At least one analytics provider is currently active on this deployment. It is used solely to understand which articles are useful and which pages are broken.'
        : 'At the time of the last update to this page, none of these were enabled, so no analytics data was being collected at all.'
    }
    We use analytics only to understand which articles are worth writing more of. We do not
    sell personal data, we do not run behavioral advertising, and we do not build
    cross-site profiles of readers.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis for processing (GDPR)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent</strong> — newsletter subscription, and any non-essential analytics
      or measurement cookies. You can withdraw consent at any time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — security logging, abuse and bot mitigation,
      and aggregate measurement of site performance. We balance this against your rights
      and keep the data minimal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contract</strong> — responding to a request you sent us, such as a directory
      submission or a partnership enquiry.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-party processors</h2>
  <p>
    We keep the list short deliberately. The services that may process data on our behalf
    are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> — hosting and content delivery. Processes request
      metadata including IP address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4 / Microsoft Clarity / Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> —
      only where configured, as described above.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Newsletter delivery provider</strong> — stores your email address and
      delivery events if you subscribe.
      <!-- Owner: name your email provider here once you have chosen one. -->
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Web font delivery</strong> — font files are requested from Google Fonts,
      which necessarily receives the request IP as part of serving the file.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers operate in the United States. Where personal data leaves the
    UK or EEA, transfers rely on the provider's standard contractual clauses or an
    equivalent adequacy mechanism.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We set no advertising cookies and no cross-site tracking cookies. The only thing stored
    by default is your light/dark theme preference, in local storage. A full breakdown,
    including the cookies our CDN sets for bot mitigation, is in the
    <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter address</strong> — until you unsubscribe, then deleted from the active list.</li>
    <li><strong>Correspondence</strong> — up to 24 months, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Directory submissions</strong> — kept while the listing is live, and for 12 months after it is removed.</li>
    <li><strong>Server and CDN logs</strong> — retained per the provider's default window, typically days rather than months.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — aggregate only, retained per the provider's configured retention period.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR, UK GDPR and comparable regimes you may request access to your personal
    data, correction of inaccurate data, deletion, restriction of processing, portability,
    and you may object to processing based on legitimate interests. You can withdraw
    consent for the newsletter at any time using the unsubscribe link in any issue.
  </p>
  <p>
    Under the CCPA/CPRA, California residents may request disclosure of the categories of
    personal information collected, request deletion, and opt out of the sale or sharing of
    personal information. <strong>We do not sell or share personal information</strong> as
    those terms are defined in the CCPA, and we do not discriminate against anyone who
    exercises a privacy right.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a> with the
    subject line beginning <code>PRIVACY</code>, or use the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We respond within 30 days. You may also complain
    to your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS with HSTS, a content security policy and modern security
    headers. Because pages are static and there is no reader database, the attack surface
    holding personal data is small. No system is perfectly secure; report a concern via the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is written for developers and technical professionals and is not directed
    at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you
    believe a child has sent us personal data, email us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change what we collect or which processors we use, we update this page and the
    "last updated" date above. Material changes will also be flagged in the newsletter.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
